<newsitem itemid="151713" id="root" date="1996-10-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Pressac year pre-tax profits rise 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Pressac year pre-tax profits rise 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.3		   vs 9.01</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.91		   vs 2.60</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.90		   vs 3.50</p>
<p> Pretax		     6.4		    vs 4.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   68.9		   vs 57.3</p>
<p> Operating result	 6.77		   vs 4.95</p>
<p>Tax			  1.94		   vs 0.6</p>
<p>Attributable	     4.22		   vs 2.99</p>
<p>Pay date		   Dec 13</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 12</p>
<p>NOTE - Pressac Holdings Plc, a supplier of electrical and electronic components, said its strong performance was attributable to improvements in market share and a substantial increase in productivity.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
